{"_id":"6a2ff9ea2204ffbc59e5a815","roadmapSlug":"python-data-analysis","nodeId":"Bk3z1CHnrnV6ii2Y0BF8G","description":"# Heatmaps\n\n`sns.heatmap()` visualizes matrix-style data using color intensity. It is most commonly used to display correlation matrices and pivot tables. Color maps, annotations, and masking options allow the heatmap to be customized for readability. Heatmaps are an effective way to show patterns across two categorical dimensions.","resources":[{"type":"official","title":"seaborn.heatmap","url":"https://seaborn.pydata.org/generated/seaborn.heatmap.html","_id":"6a75d326b0650226a50aeb47"},{"type":"article","title":"Data Visualization with Seaborn: Heatmaps","url":"https://medium.com/@1zeyneper/data-visualization-with-seaborn-heatmaps-58abfadd79d5","_id":"6a75d326b0650226a50aeb48"},{"type":"video","title":"Seaborn heatmap | How to make a heatmap in Python Seaborn and adjust the heatmap style","url":"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=0U9cs2V-Mqc","_id":"6a75d326b0650226a50aeb49"}],"createdAt":"2026-06-15T13:11:06.459Z","updatedAt":"2026-08-07T12:44:22.099Z","lessonPacks":[],"paidResources":[{"_id":"6a5e3360acf8c05faf5e1c2a","title":"DataCamp - Data Analyst with Python","partner":"DataCamp","type":"course","url":"https://datacamp.pxf.io/QY0dY9"},{"_id":"6a5e3365acf8c05faf5e1ded","title":"DataCamp - Python Data Fundamentals","partner":"DataCamp","type":"course","url":"https://datacamp.pxf.io/k4V24x"}],"contribution":"https://github.com/kamranahmedse/developer-roadmap/tree/master/roadmaps/python-data-analysis/content/Bk3z1CHnrnV6ii2Y0BF8G.md"}